11.0.0, seventh upload — play it with the phone alone

What is new since 10009. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds and, where a test
target reaches it, tests; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Keys and drum pads on the screen. Under every view sits a keyboard as wide as the screen
  holds (octave down/up, the lowest key is shown), and for a drum track the kit as eight pads,
  kick at the bottom left. The keys button in the transport hides and shows them.
- The keys play the live track, the same one a MIDI keyboard plays (choose it with the keys
  button on a track). The song's key lock applies, and a MIDI take records what you play on
  the screen, exactly as from a keyboard.
- A key held on the screen and the same key held on a MIDI keyboard are two keys: lifting
  one does not end the other, and their notes never change order on the way to the engine.
  On a phone on its side the keys and pads shrink so the tracks above keep their room; a
  short tap sounds; VoiceOver's activate plays a key.
- A first install opens Four Tracks: Keys, Bass and Lead on their sounds and a Drums track
  with an empty one-bar pattern. The first touch on the keys sounds.
- The store: closing the store page no longer marks the purchase as not owned; Restore says
  what it found; Buy and Restore wait for each other; "not on sale yet" shows only while the
  App Store knows no product.
- A plugin window shows its controls at once, with the demo note, and unlocks when the
  purchase is found; the extension asks the App Store for at most five seconds.
- Under the hood since 10009: about two hundred repairs from eight review rounds — taking a
  song file the memory cannot hold, audio takes that cannot move or load, the input opening
  only into headphones or an interface, the sampler's memory, sample-rate changes, and plugin
  sessions restored in low memory. Each names itself in the status line when it happens.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10009), sixth upload — the app survives what a device does to it (songs as one file in Files and AirDrop, launch and audio recovery, headphone unplug pauses, plugin crash reload). Before that: 11.0.0 (10008), fifth upload — the app records the plugin purchase in the App Group
group.com.echoelmusic.shared and the Audio Units read it there (factory job 002). Before that:
10007 (finding no earlier songs no longer marks the import done), 10006, 10005, 10004 (the first
Echoel Studio build). group.com.echoelmusic (the import of earlier songs) is still not requested
(F17): until it is, the import finds nothing.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. Delete Echoel, install this build, open it: Four Tracks opens, and touching a key under the
   tracks sounds within three seconds, without a MIDI keyboard. Two fingers play two notes.
2. Tap the keys button on the Drums track: the pads appear, Kick, Snare and the hats sound.
   Hide the keys with the transport's keys button and show them again.
3. Arm the Keys track, press Record, play eight bars on the screen keys, Stop: the take is a
   clip, and it plays back what you played. Pull down Notification Center mid-note: no note
   keeps sounding.
4. Choose a key and scale for the song and turn on the key lock: every screen key plays a
   note of the scale.
5. Plugin family SP1-SP3 (FOUNDER_INBOX section 2): Echoel Synth, Drums and EQ load in AUM, the
   window shows its controls at once, and without a purchase the Synth pauses 2 s every 30 s.
